    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"873350\">Weiyi Wang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/How.20do.20we.20prove.20infinity.20for.20a.20subtype.20of.20.E2.84.95.20in.20Lean.204.3F/near/579966545\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Do you have a concrete statement / <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mwe.html\">#mwe</a> we can work on?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm working on a proof that a specific subtype of <code>Nat</code> is infinite. I'm trying to prove it by showing the set is 'unbounded' (i.e., for every N, there's an element y in the set such that y &gt; N <br>\n), but I'm hitting <code>Unknown constant</code> or <code>Type mismatch</code> errors when trying to find the right Mathlib 4 theorem to bridge 'unboundedness' to the <code>Infinite</code> typeclass.<br>\nHere is my MWE. It contains some placeholder logic to keep it standalone, but it reproduces the exact error I'm stuck on: </p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- 1. Setup a basic structure and subtype</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target_E</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℤ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">structure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Cell</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">gap_is_twin</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"k\">if</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">+</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">%</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">then</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">2</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">else</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target_E</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">//</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Cell</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- 2. A placeholder for my research lemma</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">lemma</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_successor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Nonempty</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Cell</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- In my real code, this is proven via a sieve</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n<span class=\"c1\">-- 3. THE PROBLEM AREA</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S_is_infinite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Infinite</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- I want to use the logic: (∀ N, ∃ y &gt; N ∧ y ∈ S) → Infinite S</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- I've tried several names like Nat.infinite_of_unbounded or</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- Set.infinite_iff_unbounded, but they aren't working as expected.</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">apply</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">infinite_iff_unbounded</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">intro</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"c1\">-- error</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">obtain</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_gt</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_mem</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exists_successor</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">use</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟨</span><span class=\"n\">h_gt</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">h_mem</span><span class=\"bp\">⟩</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
